{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And it came between the camp of Egypt.</b> A parable: a man was walking on the road and his son was walking ahead of him. Robbers came to seize him; he took him from in front of him and put him behind him. A wolf came from behind him; he put him in front of him. Robbers came from in front of him and wolves from behind him; he put him on his shoulder and fought them all. So too: ״וְאָנֹכִי תִּרְגַּלְתִּי לְאֶפְרַיִם קָחָתִים עַל זְרוֹעֹתַי״ (Hosea 11) (Mekhilta)." "<b>And the cloud and the darkness were.</b> For Egypt." "<b>And it lit</b> the pillar of fire <b>the night</b> for Israel, and went before them as usual, to travel all the night; and the darkness of the pall was toward Egypt's side." "<b>And the one did not come near the other.</b> Camp to camp (ibid.)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:11.021110861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}